 6. 🤒 Flu comes early 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data : CDC. Chart: Jim Sergent/Axios Early signs suggest flu season is starting sooner than in recent years, Axios' Carly Mallenbaum writes from CDC data . 

 Why it matters: If you're thinking about getting your flu shot, health experts suggest it's time to roll up your sleeve. It takes about two weeks after vaccination to develop immunity. Go deeper . 

 
 
