 8. 📚 1 for the road: Record book bans 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Nearly 12,000 book bans were instituted in public schools over the past year, according to a new study from PEN America , the highest total since the organization began tracking five years ago.

 Many of the bans were in Florida and Texas, where restrictive laws have been passed. Themes of race, racism, sexuality and gender identity remain the most common reasons books are challenged. Among the titles that appeared on PEN America's Index of School Book Bans for the first time during the 2025-26 school year: Charlotte Brontë's 19th-century classic "Jane Eyre."

